This directory contains a patch intended to run DICE simulations
with the capability to restart and include additional DICE initial conditions
at restart.

The base of the patch is the DICE patch (in my case composed of the original patch in patch/init/dice and my patched version in patch/tepper/dice).

The first patch modification consists of an addition of a modified version of the case('ramses') snippet in taken from patch/init/restart/init_part.f90, available via the subroutine load_ramses.

This patch requires additions to the already dice-patched read_param.f90, and to include a patched  version of adaptive_loop.f90, init_time.f90 due to the nature if nrestart < 0.

The next, yet to to, patch modification is the addition of a code snippet in init_part.f90, identified by case('dice_restart'), which consists of a merge between the case('dice') snippet in the same file and the case('ramses') snippet in patch/init/restart, available here as via the yet to do subroutine load_dice_restart

IMPORTANT: See /Users/tepper/codes/ramses_020217/ramses/trunk/ramses/patch/mySIMS/Nbody+HD/dice/myics/dice_restart/src/init_part.f90, DICE_RESTART snippet
for a guide on how to achieve this.

The required patches should all correctly included via the appropriate make file (to be created). Note that, with luck, only init_part.f90 needs to be modified, and the patch will work by including my patches, my dice patch included. NOTE that this requires actually getting the dice_restart patch to work. Alternateively, I'll try to include the Ramses restart patch separately, which however requires modifications to several files (see patch/init/restart)

Specific modifications.

init_part.f90:
- added case('ramses') and corresponding routine load_ramses

read_param.f90:
- added restart_commons
- added restart_params
